e effective than treatment"}, {"id": "68e6d1e140568442626a30f8", "icon": "pulmonology", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy", "subheading": "Spot inflammation before symptoms appear"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "iconAccordions", "secondaryColorLayout": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}	68e6abb27b8a807323f24ee0	\N	container-small
3	128	version.layout	397	{"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "THE REALITY OF ARTHRITIS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is the leading cause of chronic pain in dogs.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Nearly half of young dogs under four years old already show osteoarthritis on x-rays.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 3, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Up to 80% of dogs over 8 years old have some degree of osteoarthritis.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It’s not limited to large breeds. Every dog owner should be thinking about joint health and prevention, regardless of their dog's breed, size, or current age.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DESCRIPTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Everything you need to know in 60 seconds:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 2, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b227865d312d30ee2fcc", "items": [{"id": "68e6b22a1a6ead44797ae1f5", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What is osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22b1a6ead44797ae1f7", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What causes osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22e1a6ead44797ae1f9", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Which dogs can get osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68fbc9679084613b277002a1", "heading": "New item"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "accordion"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b84f077c5a01f48d7ac8", "rows": [{"id": "68e6b8fafed14ef0d0962c9a", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b8fcfed14ef0d0962c9c", "value": "Changes in gait or limping"}, {"id": "68e6b8fefed14ef0d0962c9e"}]}, {"id": "68e6b90cfed14ef0d0962ca0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b90efed14ef0d0962ca2", "value": "Changes in posture or sitting position"}, {"id": "68e6b90ffed14ef0d0962ca4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b916fed14ef0d0962ca6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b918fed14ef0d0962ca8", "value": "Difficulty moving between laying, sitting, and standing"}, {"id": "68e6b91afed14ef0d0962caa"}]}, {"id": "68e6b944fed14ef0d0962cac", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b947fed14ef0d0962cae", "value": "Difficulty climbing stairs or reluctance to jump"}, {"id": "68e6b948fed14ef0d0962cb0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b952fed14ef0d0962cb2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b953fed14ef0d0962cb4", "value": "Reluctance to go on walks for as long as usual"}]}, {"id": "68e6b95afed14ef0d0962cb6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b95cfed14ef0d0962cb8", "value": "Swelling around joints"}, {"id": "68e6b95dfed14ef0d0962cba"}]}, {"id": "68e6b963fed14ef0d0962cbc", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cbe", "value": "Decreased range of motion"}, {"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cc0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b96cfed14ef0d0962cc2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b96efed14ef0d0962cc4", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints"}, {"id": "68e6b96ffed14ef0d0962cc6"}]}, {"id": "68e6b975fed14ef0d0962cc8", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b977fed14ef0d0962cca", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints Muscle loss, particularly in the thighs"}, {"id": "68e6b979fed14ef0d0962ccc"}]}, {"id": "68e6b97ffed14ef0d0962cce", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b984fed14ef0d0962cd0", "value": "Behavioral changes or increased irritability"}, {"id": "68e6b985fed14ef0d0962cd2"}]}, {"id": "68e6b987fed14ef0d0962cd4", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b98cfed14ef0d0962cd6", "value": "Changes in sleeping positions (not laying in positions they used to enjoy)"}, {"id": "68e6b98dfed14ef0d0962cd8"}]}, {"id": "68e6b990fed14ef0d0962cda", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b994fed14ef0d0962cdc", "value": "Not wanting to curl into a ball or roll around like they used to"}, {"id": "68e6b995fed14ef0d0962cde"}]}, {"id": "68e6b99bfed14ef0d0962ce0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce2", "value": "Difficulty posturing to pee or poop"}, {"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a3fed14ef0d0962ce6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9a5fed14ef0d0962ce8", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite"}, {"id": "68e6b9a7fed14ef0d0962cea"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a9fed14ef0d0962cec", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9acfed14ef0d0962cee", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}, {"id": "68e6b9affed14ef0d0962cf0", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}]}], "intro": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Dogs with arthritis often don't show obvious signs of pain, which makes it challenging for dog parents to know how much their dog is suffering. Many dogs naturally conceal discomfort, so it's important to watch for subtle changes in behavior and movement patterns. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Any stiffness after your dog has been lying down should be taken seriously, as this typically signals an underlying joint or muscle problem. The key is paying close attention to small changes in your dog's daily routine and movement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "columns": [{"id": "68e6b8e5fed14ef0d0962c96", "type": "text", "heading": "Symptoms"}, {"id": "68e6b8e7fed14ef0d0962c98", "type": "input", "heading": "Check all that apply"}], "heading": "Symptoms", "blockName": "", "blockType": "table", "rowsCount": 15, "subheading": "Keep an eye out for these signs in your dog & track any symptoms you notice.", "tableColor": "#FFBA64", "tableTitle": "Watch for these signs in your dog:", "columnsCount": 2, "backgroundColor": "#FFF4E0", "columnHeadingColor": "#FFA12F"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "These signs often become more noticeable when your dog starts moving after resting for a while. Recording videos of how your dog moves when they're young and feeling good can help you spot gradual changes over time. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If you notice any of these changes, it's time to schedule a veterinary appointment for proper evaluation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DIAGNOSTICS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It's important to remember that limping or stiffness doesn't automatically mean your dog has arthritis. Your dog could have a neurologic condition, muscle restriction, or other conditions affecting their movement. Getting X-rays to confirm arthritis is crucial before starting any treatment, particularly before using arthritis-specific medications. X-rays are performed to look for changes in the bones and to check for joint swelling.  ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Testing for osteoarthritis starts with a physical exam by your veterinarian. This will typically involve a gait analysis, which means watching carefully how your dog walks and moves to spot any problems.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6c98b5d64d0cdc81ca60f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If your vet suggests arthritis treatment based only on a physical exam, ask for X-rays first to confirm the diagnosis before beginning any medication.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "IMPORTANT", "blockName": "", "blockType": "alert", "widthConstraint": false, "fullWidthContent": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is diagnosed and staged based on the COAST Development Group guidelines from Stage 0 to Stage 4:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6ccdb90d7f57f61318fcb", "rows": [{"id": "68e6ccdc947b25accbe34d59", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, no risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 0"}, {"id": "68e6ccee947b25accbe34d5b", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, but has risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 1"}, {"id": "68e6ccfa947b25accbe34d5d", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Mild signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 2"}, {"id": "68e6cd04947b25accbe34d5f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Moderate signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 3"}, {"id": "68e6cd0e947b25accbe34d61", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Severe signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 4"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "pillRows"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Depending on your dog's condition, your vet may also perform other tests: ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Cytology of the joint where your vet will take fluid from the joint to assess the level of inflammation. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Advanced imaging like CT scans may be necessary to get a clearer picture of what's happening inside the joint.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "TREATMENT", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes. Physical rehabilitation is irreplaceable in joint disease management, focusing on targeted exercises to strengthen muscles, improve range of motion, and build endurance. The philosophy is clear: there is no pill that can replace the physical act of moving the body to repair, rebuild, and restore musculoskeletal function. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Small changes to your dog’s environment, diet, and exercise routine can greatly improve your dog’s quality of life with a joint disease.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6cfd311ea7c1a5a2e347b", "items": [{"id": "68e6cfd5486f08c805e5c062", "icon": "massage", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Physical Rehabilitation", "subheading": "Maintaining ideal weight is the #1 factor"}, {"id": "68e6d0f9486f08c805e5c064", "icon": "bolt", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pulsed Electromagnetic Field (PEMF)", "subheading": "Early detection prevents severe progression"}, {"id": "68e6d13fc1b2f40e0fb80f9f", "icon": "acupuncture", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Acupuncture", "subheading": "Right exercise builds strength without damage"}, {"id": "68e6d157c1b2f40e0fb80fa1", "icon": "air", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Ozone Therapy", "subheading": "Proper nail length maintains healthy joints"}, {"id": "68e6d19aba94a2830080939e", "icon": "water", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Chiropractic Care", "subheading": "Timing affects joint development"}, {"id": "68e6d1c240568442626a30f4", "icon": "pill", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pharmaceuticals", "subheading": "Simple changes prevent slips, trips, and falls"}, {"id": "68e6d1cf40568442626a30f6", "icon": "sunny", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Laser Therapy", "subheading": "Prevention is more effective than treatment"}, {"id": "68e6d1e140568442626a30f8", "icon": "pulmonology", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy", "subheading": "Spot inflammation before symptoms appear"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "iconAccordions", "secondaryColorLayout": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}}	68e6abb27b8a807323f24ee0	\N	container-small
3	135	version.layout	413	{"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "THE REALITY OF ARTHRITIS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is the leading cause of chronic pain in dogs.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Nearly half of young dogs under four years old already show osteoarthritis on x-rays.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 3, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Up to 80% of dogs over 8 years old have some degree of osteoarthritis.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It’s not limited to large breeds. Every dog owner should be thinking about joint health and prevention, regardless of their dog's breed, size, or current age.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DESCRIPTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Everything you need to know in 60 seconds:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 2, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b227865d312d30ee2fcc", "items": [{"id": "68e6b22a1a6ead44797ae1f5", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What is osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22b1a6ead44797ae1f7", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What causes osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22e1a6ead44797ae1f9", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Which dogs can get osteoarthritis?"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "accordion"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b84f077c5a01f48d7ac8", "rows": [{"id": "68e6b8fafed14ef0d0962c9a", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b8fcfed14ef0d0962c9c", "value": "Changes in gait or limping"}, {"id": "68e6b8fefed14ef0d0962c9e"}]}, {"id": "68e6b90cfed14ef0d0962ca0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b90efed14ef0d0962ca2", "value": "Changes in posture or sitting position"}, {"id": "68e6b90ffed14ef0d0962ca4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b916fed14ef0d0962ca6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b918fed14ef0d0962ca8", "value": "Difficulty moving between laying, sitting, and standing"}, {"id": "68e6b91afed14ef0d0962caa"}]}, {"id": "68e6b944fed14ef0d0962cac", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b947fed14ef0d0962cae", "value": "Difficulty climbing stairs or reluctance to jump"}, {"id": "68e6b948fed14ef0d0962cb0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b952fed14ef0d0962cb2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b953fed14ef0d0962cb4", "value": "Reluctance to go on walks for as long as usual"}]}, {"id": "68e6b95afed14ef0d0962cb6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b95cfed14ef0d0962cb8", "value": "Swelling around joints"}, {"id": "68e6b95dfed14ef0d0962cba"}]}, {"id": "68e6b963fed14ef0d0962cbc", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cbe", "value": "Decreased range of motion"}, {"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cc0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b96cfed14ef0d0962cc2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b96efed14ef0d0962cc4", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints"}, {"id": "68e6b96ffed14ef0d0962cc6"}]}, {"id": "68e6b975fed14ef0d0962cc8", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b977fed14ef0d0962cca", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints Muscle loss, particularly in the thighs"}, {"id": "68e6b979fed14ef0d0962ccc"}]}, {"id": "68e6b97ffed14ef0d0962cce", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b984fed14ef0d0962cd0", "value": "Behavioral changes or increased irritability"}, {"id": "68e6b985fed14ef0d0962cd2"}]}, {"id": "68e6b987fed14ef0d0962cd4", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b98cfed14ef0d0962cd6", "value": "Changes in sleeping positions (not laying in positions they used to enjoy)"}, {"id": "68e6b98dfed14ef0d0962cd8"}]}, {"id": "68e6b990fed14ef0d0962cda", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b994fed14ef0d0962cdc", "value": "Not wanting to curl into a ball or roll around like they used to"}, {"id": "68e6b995fed14ef0d0962cde"}]}, {"id": "68e6b99bfed14ef0d0962ce0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce2", "value": "Difficulty posturing to pee or poop"}, {"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a3fed14ef0d0962ce6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9a5fed14ef0d0962ce8", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite"}, {"id": "68e6b9a7fed14ef0d0962cea"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a9fed14ef0d0962cec", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9acfed14ef0d0962cee", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}, {"id": "68e6b9affed14ef0d0962cf0", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}]}], "intro": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Dogs with arthritis often don't show obvious signs of pain, which makes it challenging for dog parents to know how much their dog is suffering. Many dogs naturally conceal discomfort, so it's important to watch for subtle changes in behavior and movement patterns. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Any stiffness after your dog has been lying down should be taken seriously, as this typically signals an underlying joint or muscle problem. The key is paying close attention to small changes in your dog's daily routine and movement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "columns": [{"id": "68e6b8e5fed14ef0d0962c96", "type": "text", "heading": "Symptoms"}, {"id": "68e6b8e7fed14ef0d0962c98", "type": "input", "heading": "Check all that apply"}], "heading": "Symptoms", "blockName": "", "blockType": "table", "subheading": "Keep an eye out for these signs in your dog & track any symptoms you notice.", "tableColor": "#FFBA64", "tableTitle": "Watch for these signs in your dog:", "tableOverflow": "overflow", "backgroundColor": "#FFF4E0", "columnHeadingColor": "#FFA12F"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "These signs often become more noticeable when your dog starts moving after resting for a while. Recording videos of how your dog moves when they're young and feeling good can help you spot gradual changes over time. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If you notice any of these changes, it's time to schedule a veterinary appointment for proper evaluation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DIAGNOSTICS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It's important to remember that limping or stiffness doesn't automatically mean your dog has arthritis. Your dog could have a neurologic condition, muscle restriction, or other conditions affecting their movement. Getting X-rays to confirm arthritis is crucial before starting any treatment, particularly before using arthritis-specific medications. X-rays are performed to look for changes in the bones and to check for joint swelling.  ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Testing for osteoarthritis starts with a physical exam by your veterinarian. This will typically involve a gait analysis, which means watching carefully how your dog walks and moves to spot any problems.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6c98b5d64d0cdc81ca60f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If your vet suggests arthritis treatment based only on a physical exam, ask for X-rays first to confirm the diagnosis before beginning any medication.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "IMPORTANT", "blockName": "", "blockType": "alert", "alertOverflow": "overflow", "widthConstraint": false, "fullWidthContent": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is diagnosed and staged based on the COAST Development Group guidelines from Stage 0 to Stage 4:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6ccdb90d7f57f61318fcb", "rows": [{"id": "68e6ccdc947b25accbe34d59", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, no risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 0"}, {"id": "68e6ccee947b25accbe34d5b", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, but has risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 1"}, {"id": "68e6ccfa947b25accbe34d5d", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Mild signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 2"}, {"id": "68e6cd04947b25accbe34d5f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Moderate signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 3"}, {"id": "68e6cd0e947b25accbe34d61", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Severe signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 4"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "pillRows"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Depending on your dog's condition, your vet may also perform other tests: ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Cytology of the joint where your vet will take fluid from the joint to assess the level of inflammation. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Advanced imaging like CT scans may be necessary to get a clearer picture of what's happening inside the joint.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "TREATMENT", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes. Physical rehabilitation is irreplaceable in joint disease management, focusing on targeted exercises to strengthen muscles, improve range of motion, and build endurance. The philosophy is clear: there is no pill that can replace the physical act of moving the body to repair, rebuild, and restore musculoskeletal function. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Small changes to your dog’s environment, diet, and exercise routine can greatly improve your dog’s quality of life with a joint disease.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6cfd311ea7c1a5a2e347b", "items": [{"id": "68e6cfd5486f08c805e5c062", "icon": "massage", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Physical Rehabilitation", "subheading": "Maintaining ideal weight is the #1 factor"}, {"id": "68e6d0f9486f08c805e5c064", "icon": "bolt", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pulsed Electromagnetic Field (PEMF)", "subheading": "Early detection prevents severe progression"}, {"id": "68e6d13fc1b2f40e0fb80f9f", "icon": "acupuncture", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Acupuncture", "subheading": "Right exercise builds strength without damage"}, {"id": "68e6d157c1b2f40e0fb80fa1", "icon": "air", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Ozone Therapy", "subheading": "Proper nail length maintains healthy joints"}, {"id": "68e6d19aba94a2830080939e", "icon": "water", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Chiropractic Care", "subheading": "Timing affects joint development"}, {"id": "68e6d1c240568442626a30f4", "icon": "pill", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pharmaceuticals", "subheading": "Simple changes prevent slips, trips, and falls"}, {"id": "68e6d1cf40568442626a30f6", "icon": "sunny", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Laser Therapy", "subheading": "Prevention is more effective than treatment"}, {"id": "68e6d1e140568442626a30f8", "icon": "pulmonology", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy", "subheading": "Spot inflammation before symptoms appear"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "iconAccordions", "secondaryColorLayout": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}	68e6abb27b8a807323f24ee0	\N	container-small
3	136	version.layout	414	{"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "THE REALITY OF ARTHRITIS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is the leading cause of chronic pain in dogs.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Nearly half of young dogs under four years old already show osteoarthritis on x-rays.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 3, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Up to 80% of dogs over 8 years old have some degree of osteoarthritis.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It’s not limited to large breeds. Every dog owner should be thinking about joint health and prevention, regardless of their dog's breed, size, or current age.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DESCRIPTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Everything you need to know in 60 seconds:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 2, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b227865d312d30ee2fcc", "items": [{"id": "68e6b22a1a6ead44797ae1f5", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What is osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22b1a6ead44797ae1f7", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What causes osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22e1a6ead44797ae1f9", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Which dogs can get osteoarthritis?"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "accordion"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b84f077c5a01f48d7ac8", "rows": [{"id": "68e6b8fafed14ef0d0962c9a", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b8fcfed14ef0d0962c9c", "value": "Changes in gait or limping"}, {"id": "68e6b8fefed14ef0d0962c9e"}]}, {"id": "68e6b90cfed14ef0d0962ca0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b90efed14ef0d0962ca2", "value": "Changes in posture or sitting position"}, {"id": "68e6b90ffed14ef0d0962ca4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b916fed14ef0d0962ca6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b918fed14ef0d0962ca8", "value": "Difficulty moving between laying, sitting, and standing"}, {"id": "68e6b91afed14ef0d0962caa"}]}, {"id": "68e6b944fed14ef0d0962cac", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b947fed14ef0d0962cae", "value": "Difficulty climbing stairs or reluctance to jump"}, {"id": "68e6b948fed14ef0d0962cb0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b952fed14ef0d0962cb2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b953fed14ef0d0962cb4", "value": "Reluctance to go on walks for as long as usual"}]}, {"id": "68e6b95afed14ef0d0962cb6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b95cfed14ef0d0962cb8", "value": "Swelling around joints"}, {"id": "68e6b95dfed14ef0d0962cba"}]}, {"id": "68e6b963fed14ef0d0962cbc", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cbe", "value": "Decreased range of motion"}, {"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cc0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b96cfed14ef0d0962cc2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b96efed14ef0d0962cc4", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints"}, {"id": "68e6b96ffed14ef0d0962cc6"}]}, {"id": "68e6b975fed14ef0d0962cc8", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b977fed14ef0d0962cca", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints Muscle loss, particularly in the thighs"}, {"id": "68e6b979fed14ef0d0962ccc"}]}, {"id": "68e6b97ffed14ef0d0962cce", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b984fed14ef0d0962cd0", "value": "Behavioral changes or increased irritability"}, {"id": "68e6b985fed14ef0d0962cd2"}]}, {"id": "68e6b987fed14ef0d0962cd4", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b98cfed14ef0d0962cd6", "value": "Changes in sleeping positions (not laying in positions they used to enjoy)"}, {"id": "68e6b98dfed14ef0d0962cd8"}]}, {"id": "68e6b990fed14ef0d0962cda", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b994fed14ef0d0962cdc", "value": "Not wanting to curl into a ball or roll around like they used to"}, {"id": "68e6b995fed14ef0d0962cde"}]}, {"id": "68e6b99bfed14ef0d0962ce0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce2", "value": "Difficulty posturing to pee or poop"}, {"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a3fed14ef0d0962ce6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9a5fed14ef0d0962ce8", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite"}, {"id": "68e6b9a7fed14ef0d0962cea"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a9fed14ef0d0962cec", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9acfed14ef0d0962cee", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}, {"id": "68e6b9affed14ef0d0962cf0", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}]}], "intro": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Dogs with arthritis often don't show obvious signs of pain, which makes it challenging for dog parents to know how much their dog is suffering. Many dogs naturally conceal discomfort, so it's important to watch for subtle changes in behavior and movement patterns. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Any stiffness after your dog has been lying down should be taken seriously, as this typically signals an underlying joint or muscle problem. The key is paying close attention to small changes in your dog's daily routine and movement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "columns": [{"id": "68e6b8e5fed14ef0d0962c96", "type": "text", "heading": "Symptoms"}, {"id": "68e6b8e7fed14ef0d0962c98", "type": "input", "heading": "Check all that apply"}], "heading": "Symptoms", "blockName": "", "blockType": "table", "subheading": "Keep an eye out for these signs in your dog & track any symptoms you notice.", "tableColor": "#FFBA64", "tableTitle": "Watch for these signs in your dog:", "tableOverflow": "overflow", "backgroundColor": "#FFF4E0", "columnHeadingColor": "#FFA12F"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "These signs often become more noticeable when your dog starts moving after resting for a while. Recording videos of how your dog moves when they're young and feeling good can help you spot gradual changes over time. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If you notice any of these changes, it's time to schedule a veterinary appointment for proper evaluation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DIAGNOSTICS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It's important to remember that limping or stiffness doesn't automatically mean your dog has arthritis. Your dog could have a neurologic condition, muscle restriction, or other conditions affecting their movement. Getting X-rays to confirm arthritis is crucial before starting any treatment, particularly before using arthritis-specific medications. X-rays are performed to look for changes in the bones and to check for joint swelling.  ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Testing for osteoarthritis starts with a physical exam by your veterinarian. This will typically involve a gait analysis, which means watching carefully how your dog walks and moves to spot any problems.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6c98b5d64d0cdc81ca60f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If your vet suggests arthritis treatment based only on a physical exam, ask for X-rays first to confirm the diagnosis before beginning any medication.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "IMPORTANT", "blockName": "", "blockType": "alert", "alertOverflow": "overflow", "widthConstraint": false, "fullWidthContent": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is diagnosed and staged based on the COAST Development Group guidelines from Stage 0 to Stage 4:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6ccdb90d7f57f61318fcb", "rows": [{"id": "68e6ccdc947b25accbe34d59", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, no risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 0"}, {"id": "68e6ccee947b25accbe34d5b", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, but has risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 1"}, {"id": "68e6ccfa947b25accbe34d5d", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Mild signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 2"}, {"id": "68e6cd04947b25accbe34d5f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Moderate signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 3"}, {"id": "68e6cd0e947b25accbe34d61", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Severe signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 4"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "pillRows"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Depending on your dog's condition, your vet may also perform other tests: ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Cytology of the joint where your vet will take fluid from the joint to assess the level of inflammation. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Advanced imaging like CT scans may be necessary to get a clearer picture of what's happening inside the joint.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "TREATMENT", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes. Physical rehabilitation is irreplaceable in joint disease management, focusing on targeted exercises to strengthen muscles, improve range of motion, and build endurance. The philosophy is clear: there is no pill that can replace the physical act of moving the body to repair, rebuild, and restore musculoskeletal function. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Small changes to your dog’s environment, diet, and exercise routine can greatly improve your dog’s quality of life with a joint disease.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6cfd311ea7c1a5a2e347b", "items": [{"id": "68e6cfd5486f08c805e5c062", "icon": "massage", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Physical Rehabilitation", "subheading": "Maintaining ideal weight is the #1 factor"}, {"id": "68e6d0f9486f08c805e5c064", "icon": "bolt", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pulsed Electromagnetic Field (PEMF)", "subheading": "Early detection prevents severe progression"}, {"id": "68e6d13fc1b2f40e0fb80f9f", "icon": "acupuncture", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Acupuncture", "subheading": "Right exercise builds strength without damage"}, {"id": "68e6d157c1b2f40e0fb80fa1", "icon": "air", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Ozone Therapy", "subheading": "Proper nail length maintains healthy joints"}, {"id": "68e6d19aba94a2830080939e", "icon": "water", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Chiropractic Care", "subheading": "Timing affects joint development"}, {"id": "68e6d1c240568442626a30f4", "icon": "pill", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pharmaceuticals", "subheading": "Simple changes prevent slips, trips, and falls"}, {"id": "68e6d1cf40568442626a30f6", "icon": "sunny", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Laser Therapy", "subheading": "Prevention is more effective than treatment"}, {"id": "68e6d1e140568442626a30f8", "icon": "pulmonology", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy", "subheading": "Spot inflammation before symptoms appear"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "iconAccordions", "secondaryColorLayout": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}	68e6abb27b8a807323f24ee0	\N	container-small
3	130	version.layout	407	{"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "THE REALITY OF ARTHRITIS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is the leading cause of chronic pain in dogs.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Nearly half of young dogs under four years old already show osteoarthritis on x-rays.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 3, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Up to 80% of dogs over 8 years old have some degree of osteoarthritis.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It’s not limited to large breeds. Every dog owner should be thinking about joint health and prevention, regardless of their dog's breed, size, or current age.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DESCRIPTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Everything you need to know in 60 seconds:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 2, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b227865d312d30ee2fcc", "items": [{"id": "68e6b22a1a6ead44797ae1f5", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What is osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22b1a6ead44797ae1f7", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "What causes osteoarthritis?"}, {"id": "68e6b22e1a6ead44797ae1f9", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis can affect any dog, regardless of their breed, whether they are male or female, and at any age. For dogs that live into their senior years, joint degeneration is expected. What matters most is how quickly it progresses and when we need to step in with supportive care. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Many cases of osteoarthritis are preventable or can be significantly delayed through proper early care, appropriate exercise, weight management, and avoiding early trauma or hormonal disruption.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Which dogs can get osteoarthritis?"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "accordion"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 2}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6b84f077c5a01f48d7ac8", "rows": [{"id": "68e6b8fafed14ef0d0962c9a", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b8fcfed14ef0d0962c9c", "value": "Changes in gait or limping"}, {"id": "68e6b8fefed14ef0d0962c9e"}]}, {"id": "68e6b90cfed14ef0d0962ca0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b90efed14ef0d0962ca2", "value": "Changes in posture or sitting position"}, {"id": "68e6b90ffed14ef0d0962ca4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b916fed14ef0d0962ca6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b918fed14ef0d0962ca8", "value": "Difficulty moving between laying, sitting, and standing"}, {"id": "68e6b91afed14ef0d0962caa"}]}, {"id": "68e6b944fed14ef0d0962cac", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b947fed14ef0d0962cae", "value": "Difficulty climbing stairs or reluctance to jump"}, {"id": "68e6b948fed14ef0d0962cb0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b952fed14ef0d0962cb2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b953fed14ef0d0962cb4", "value": "Reluctance to go on walks for as long as usual"}]}, {"id": "68e6b95afed14ef0d0962cb6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b95cfed14ef0d0962cb8", "value": "Swelling around joints"}, {"id": "68e6b95dfed14ef0d0962cba"}]}, {"id": "68e6b963fed14ef0d0962cbc", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cbe", "value": "Decreased range of motion"}, {"id": "68e6b965fed14ef0d0962cc0"}]}, {"id": "68e6b96cfed14ef0d0962cc2", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b96efed14ef0d0962cc4", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints"}, {"id": "68e6b96ffed14ef0d0962cc6"}]}, {"id": "68e6b975fed14ef0d0962cc8", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b977fed14ef0d0962cca", "value": "Popping sounds (crepitus) in joints Muscle loss, particularly in the thighs"}, {"id": "68e6b979fed14ef0d0962ccc"}]}, {"id": "68e6b97ffed14ef0d0962cce", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b984fed14ef0d0962cd0", "value": "Behavioral changes or increased irritability"}, {"id": "68e6b985fed14ef0d0962cd2"}]}, {"id": "68e6b987fed14ef0d0962cd4", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b98cfed14ef0d0962cd6", "value": "Changes in sleeping positions (not laying in positions they used to enjoy)"}, {"id": "68e6b98dfed14ef0d0962cd8"}]}, {"id": "68e6b990fed14ef0d0962cda", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b994fed14ef0d0962cdc", "value": "Not wanting to curl into a ball or roll around like they used to"}, {"id": "68e6b995fed14ef0d0962cde"}]}, {"id": "68e6b99bfed14ef0d0962ce0", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce2", "value": "Difficulty posturing to pee or poop"}, {"id": "68e6b99dfed14ef0d0962ce4"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a3fed14ef0d0962ce6", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9a5fed14ef0d0962ce8", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite"}, {"id": "68e6b9a7fed14ef0d0962cea"}]}, {"id": "68e6b9a9fed14ef0d0962cec", "cells": [{"id": "68e6b9acfed14ef0d0962cee", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}, {"id": "68e6b9affed14ef0d0962cf0", "value": "Reduced energy and appetite Signs of pain when touched"}]}], "intro": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Dogs with arthritis often don't show obvious signs of pain, which makes it challenging for dog parents to know how much their dog is suffering. Many dogs naturally conceal discomfort, so it's important to watch for subtle changes in behavior and movement patterns. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Any stiffness after your dog has been lying down should be taken seriously, as this typically signals an underlying joint or muscle problem. The key is paying close attention to small changes in your dog's daily routine and movement.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "columns": [{"id": "68e6b8e5fed14ef0d0962c96", "type": "text", "heading": "Symptoms"}, {"id": "68e6b8e7fed14ef0d0962c98", "type": "input", "heading": "Check all that apply"}], "heading": "Symptoms", "blockName": "", "blockType": "table", "rowsCount": 15, "subheading": "Keep an eye out for these signs in your dog & track any symptoms you notice.", "tableColor": "#FFBA64", "tableTitle": "Watch for these signs in your dog:", "columnsCount": 2, "backgroundColor": "#FFF4E0", "columnHeadingColor": "#FFA12F"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "These signs often become more noticeable when your dog starts moving after resting for a while. Recording videos of how your dog moves when they're young and feeling good can help you spot gradual changes over time. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If you notice any of these changes, it's time to schedule a veterinary appointment for proper evaluation.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DIAGNOSTICS", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It's important to remember that limping or stiffness doesn't automatically mean your dog has arthritis. Your dog could have a neurologic condition, muscle restriction, or other conditions affecting their movement. Getting X-rays to confirm arthritis is crucial before starting any treatment, particularly before using arthritis-specific medications. X-rays are performed to look for changes in the bones and to check for joint swelling.  ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Testing for osteoarthritis starts with a physical exam by your veterinarian. This will typically involve a gait analysis, which means watching carefully how your dog walks and moves to spot any problems.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6c98b5d64d0cdc81ca60f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If your vet suggests arthritis treatment based only on a physical exam, ask for X-rays first to confirm the diagnosis before beginning any medication.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "IMPORTANT", "blockName": "", "blockType": "alert", "widthConstraint": false, "fullWidthContent": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Osteoarthritis is diagnosed and staged based on the COAST Development Group guidelines from Stage 0 to Stage 4:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6ccdb90d7f57f61318fcb", "rows": [{"id": "68e6ccdc947b25accbe34d59", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, no risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 0"}, {"id": "68e6ccee947b25accbe34d5b", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal, but has risk factors (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 1"}, {"id": "68e6ccfa947b25accbe34d5d", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Mild signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 2"}, {"id": "68e6cd04947b25accbe34d5f", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Moderate signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 3"}, {"id": "68e6cd0e947b25accbe34d61", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Severe signs (input a few examples)", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Stage 4"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "pillRows"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Depending on your dog's condition, your vet may also perform other tests: ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Cytology of the joint where your vet will take fluid from the joint to assess the level of inflammation. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Advanced imaging like CT scans may be necessary to get a clearer picture of what's happening inside the joint.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "bullet", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "TREATMENT", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes. Physical rehabilitation is irreplaceable in joint disease management, focusing on targeted exercises to strengthen muscles, improve range of motion, and build endurance. The philosophy is clear: there is no pill that can replace the physical act of moving the body to repair, rebuild, and restore musculoskeletal function. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Small changes to your dog’s environment, diet, and exercise routine can greatly improve your dog’s quality of life with a joint disease.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68e6cfd311ea7c1a5a2e347b", "items": [{"id": "68e6cfd5486f08c805e5c062", "icon": "massage", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Physical Rehabilitation", "subheading": "Maintaining ideal weight is the #1 factor"}, {"id": "68e6d0f9486f08c805e5c064", "icon": "bolt", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pulsed Electromagnetic Field (PEMF)", "subheading": "Early detection prevents severe progression"}, {"id": "68e6d13fc1b2f40e0fb80f9f", "icon": "acupuncture", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Acupuncture", "subheading": "Right exercise builds strength without damage"}, {"id": "68e6d157c1b2f40e0fb80fa1", "icon": "air", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Ozone Therapy", "subheading": "Proper nail length maintains healthy joints"}, {"id": "68e6d19aba94a2830080939e", "icon": "water", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve