3	56	version.layout	373	{"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "INTRODUCTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Joint disease is one of the leading causes of chronic pain in dogs today, yet many of the risk factors are entirely preventable through informed early intervention. As a dog parent, you have more control over your dog's joint health than you might think. Simple lifestyle choices throughout the different stages of your dog’s life can slow joint damage and keep your dog moving well.  ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Being proactive with nutrition, controlled exercise, and lifelong joint support is far more effective than waiting until your dog is already showing signs of stiffness or lameness. Pain often doesn’t look like limping or crying out. It may look like subtle weight shifts, compensatory movements, and inefficient gaiting. These are ways that dogs learn to cope with their pain. Investigating any potential pain or discomfort should be part of every dog’s care, and should be revisited often.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f2998b3aab1650e1c7560b", "tabs": [{"id": "68f299c588024ff279ce7f1f", "rows": [{"id": "68f29a6488024ff279ce7f33", "cells": [{"id": "68f29a6688024ff279ce7f35", "value": "Slowing down on walks, sleeping more, decreased activity and playtime"}, {"id": "68f29a6888024ff279ce7f37"}, {"id": "68f29a6d88024ff279ce7f39", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29a7188024ff279ce7f3b", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29afc88024ff279ce7f5d", "cells": [{"id": "68f29afe88024ff279ce7f5f", "value": "Taking longer to go from laying down to standing"}, {"id": "68f29b0188024ff279ce7f61", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b0288024ff279ce7f63", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b0588024ff279ce7f65", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b2488024ff279ce7f6b", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b2488024ff279ce7f6c", "value": "Changes in sleeping positions (can't curl into a ball anymore, stops lying on their back)"}, {"id": "68f29b2488024ff279ce7f6d", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b2488024ff279ce7f6e", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b2488024ff279ce7f6f", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b4088024ff279ce7f75", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b4088024ff279ce7f76", "value": "Quick paw shaking after standing up"}, {"id": "68f29b4088024ff279ce7f77", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b4088024ff279ce7f78", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b4088024ff279ce7f79", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b4988024ff279ce7f7f", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b4988024ff279ce7f80", "value": "Muscle loss, particularly in thigh muscles"}, {"id": "68f29b4988024ff279ce7f81", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b4988024ff279ce7f82", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b4988024ff279ce7f83", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b5288024ff279ce7f89", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b5288024ff279ce7f8a", "value": "Restlessness, can't get comfortable, shifts positions in bed, has difficulty settling down"}, {"id": "68f29b5288024ff279ce7f8b", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b5288024ff279ce7f8c", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b5288024ff279ce7f8d", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b5888024ff279ce7f93", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b5888024ff279ce7f94", "value": "Shaking (not from cold), reluctant to move"}, {"id": "68f29b5888024ff279ce7f95", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b5888024ff279ce7f96", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b5888024ff279ce7f97", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b6088024ff279ce7f9d", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b6088024ff279ce7f9e", "value": "Hesitating before stairs or jumping on furniture"}, {"id": "68f29b6088024ff279ce7f9f", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b6088024ff279ce7fa0", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b6088024ff279ce7fa1", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b6d88024ff279ce7fa7", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b6d88024ff279ce7fa8", "value": "Behavior changes (anxiety, hiding, loss of appetite, aggression, resource guarding)"}, {"id": "68f29b6d88024ff279ce7fa9", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b6d88024ff279ce7faa", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b6d88024ff279ce7fab", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "68f29b7688024ff279ce7fb1", "cells": [{"id": "68f29b7688024ff279ce7fb2", "value": "Slipping on floors, such as losing their footing on hardwood, tile, or slick floors"}, {"id": "68f29b7688024ff279ce7fb3", "value": ""}, {"id": "68f29b7688024ff279ce7fb4", "selectedValue": "Rarely"}, {"id": "68f29b7688024ff279ce7fb5", "value": "", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}], "title": "GENERAL SIGNS OF PAIN", "columns": [{"id": "68f299d288024ff279ce7f21", "type": "text", "heading": "Symptom", "mobileWidth": "", "desktopWidth": "", "selectOptions": []}, {"id": "68f299e988024ff279ce7f23", "type": "checkbox", "heading": "Observed?", "mobileWidth": "", "desktopWidth": "18%", "selectOptions": []}, {"id": "68f29a0788024ff279ce7f25", "type": "select", "heading": "How Often?", "mobileWidth": "", "desktopWidth": "18%", "selectOptions": [{"id": "68f29a1688024ff279ce7f27", "label": "Rarely", "value": "Rarel