nutrition", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Monitor treats to be less than 10% of daily calories ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 5, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Regular vet checks to establish ideal weight targets and catch weight gain early", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "number", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}}, "heading": "Digital Thermal Imaging", "subheading": "Spot inflammation before symptoms appear"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "iconAccordions", "secondaryColorLayout": true}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DIET", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Diet plays a fundamental role in your dog’s joint health. Feeding an inflammatory diet is going to increase inflammation in the body and impact your dog’s mobility. For optimal joint health, focus on reducing whole-body inflammation through diet. Switching from highly processed foods to fresh diets is one of the quickest ways to improve mobility by eliminating the daily inflammatory burden on your dog’s body. Fresh, varied diets support healthy microbiome development, while ultra-processed foods damage gut bacteria and create chronic inflammation throughout the body. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "There are several foods and supplements that have shown to prove to be helpful for joints:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f18786577f756260829d52", "items": [], "heading": "Slider", "blockName": "", "blockType": "collectionItemSlider", "usePlaceholders": true, "widthConstraint": true, "placeholderCount": 5, "placeholderImage": 2, "placeholderTitle": "Name"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "MANAGEMENT", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When your dog is living with joint disease, a multimodal approach can significantly improve their quality of life and may even reduce dependence on pharmaceutical interventions. The goal shifts from prevention to managing existing conditions while supporting the body's natural healing processes. Physical rehabilitation is irreplaceable in joint disease management, focusing on targeted exercises to strengthen muscles, improve range of motion, and build endurance. The philosophy is clear: there is no pill that can replace the physical act of moving the body to repair, rebuild, and restore musculoskeletal function.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "Small changes to your dog’s environment, diet, and exercise routine can greatly improve your dog’s quality of life with a joint disease.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f18811577f756260829d53", "items": [{"id": "68f188122b163d67b225776e", "icon": "massage", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Physical Rehabilitation", "subheading": "Maintaining ideal weight is the #1 factor"}, {"id": "68f1882a2b163d67b2257770", "icon": "bolt", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pulsed Electromagnetic Field (PEMF)", "subheading": "Early detection prevents severe progression"}, {"id": "68f188362b163d67b2257772", "icon": "acupuncture", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Acupuncture", "subheading": "Right exercise builds strength without damage"}, {"id": "68f188452b163d67b2257774", "icon": "air", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Ozone Therapy", "subheading": "Proper nail length maintains healthy joints"}, {"id": "68f188542b163d67b2257776", "icon": "water", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Chiropractic Care", "subheading": "Timing affects joint development"}, {"id": "68f188612b163d67b2257778", "icon": "pill", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Pharmaceuticals", "subheading": "Simple changes prevent slips, trips, and falls"}, {"id": "68f188702b163d67b225777a", "icon": "sunny", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Laser Therapy", "subheading": "Prevention is more effective than treatment"}, {"id": "68f188812b163d67b225777c", "icon": "pulmonology", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lorem Ipsum.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}, "heading": "Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy", "subheading": "Spot inflammation before symptoms appear"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "iconAccordions", "secondaryColorLayout": false}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f18898577f756260829d54", "items": [], "heading": "Slider", "blockName": "", "blockType": "collectionItemSlider", "usePlaceholders": true, "widthConstraint": true, "placeholderCount": 5, "placeholderImage": 2, "placeholderTitle": "Osteoarthritis"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}	68f185df2b163d67b225775c	\N	container
3	127	version.layout	735	{"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "INTRODUCTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "While advances in veterinary medicine are extending our dogs' lives in many areas, obesity remains one of the most significant threats to their health and longevity. A 14-year lifetime study researched the effects that diet restriction had on lifespan and age-related changes in dogs. It revealed that overweight and obesity alone reduces dogs' lifespans by at least two years. Maintaining your dog's ideal body condition and muscle mass is one of the most powerful commitments you can make to their health. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Obesity is a disease of chronic inflammation because fat is pro-inflammatory. While we often focus on how excess weight affects joints, the reality is that obesity leads to many other diseases throughout your dog’s body that aren’t always visible. Even a few extra pounds on your dog increases cancer risk and accelerates the development of heart failure, kidney disease, diabetes, and more. Keeping your dog at a healthy, lean body weight helps prevent these conditions and increases their overall quality of life.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "RISK ASSESSMENT", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Check all symptoms you’ve noticed to discuss at your next vet appointment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 3, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 3}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f2998b3aab1650e1c7560b", "tabs": [{"id": "68f299c588024ff279ce7f1f", "rows": [{"id": "68f29a6488024ff279ce7f33", "cells": [{"id": "68f29a6688024ff279ce7f35", "value": "Ribs are difficult to feel or buried under a thick fat layer"}, {"id": "68f29a6888024ff279ce7f37"}, {"id": "68f29a7188024ff279ce7f3b", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "690bc8815641261577378157", "cells": [{"id": "690bc8815641261577378158", "value": "Fat deposits near hips and base of tail"}, {"id": "690bc8815641261577378159"}, {"id": "690bc881564126157737815a", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "690bc886564126157737815f", "cells": [{"id": "690bc8865641261577378160", "value": "Spine is difficult to feel"}, {"id": "690bc8865641261577378161"}, {"id": "690bc8865641261577378162", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "690bc88e5641261577378167", "cells": [{"id": "690bc88e5641261577378168", "value": "Hips are rounded or hard to detect"}, {"id": "690bc88e5641261577378169"}, {"id": "690bc88e564126157737816a", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "690bc8a65641261577378177", "cells": [{"id": "690bc8a65641261577378178", "value": "Flat or sagging belly when viewed from the side"}, {"id": "690bc8a65641261577378179"}, {"id": "690bc8a6564126157737817a", "selectedValue": "Mild"}]}, {"id": "690bc89f564126157737816f", "cells": [{"id": "690bc89f5641261577378170", "value"