rsion": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Joint health problems often develop silently long before dogs show obvious signs of discomfort, making early prevention crucial for maintaining your dog's mobility throughout their life. Prevention of aging starts early in your dog’s life. Proactive care during puppyhood and young adulthood can prevent or significantly delay the onset of joint problems later in life. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is a fundamental shift in veterinary medicine to move from reactive treatment to proactive prevention, especially during a puppy’s critical developmental window. Research from UC Davis tracking over 35,000 dogs across multiple breeds demonstrates that environmental factors during the first 18 months can influence joint health outcomes for a dog's entire lifetime. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "While we cannot prevent all joint problems due to genetic factors, we can significantly influence their severity and timing through proactive care. The goal is to maximize both the quantity and quality of your dog's active years. The most effective joint health prevention plan combines multiple strategies:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f186cf577f756260829d51", "items": [{"id": "68f186d12b163d67b225775e", "icon": "balance", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Why It Matters", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": ": ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "Maintaining an ideal body weight throughout your dog's entire life is one of the most critical factors in joint health prevention. Excess weight puts additional mechanical stress on joints, increases inflammation throughout the body, accelerates cartilage breakdown, and significantly worsens arthritis progression.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "What You Can Do", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": ": ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 1}, {"tag": "ol", "type": "list", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Weigh your dog regularly, especially during growth phases and senior years", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Learn body condition scoring at home to feel for ribs and assess waist visibility", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 3, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Adjust your dog’s diet based on activity level and lifestage, while ensuring they are still receiving adequate nutrition", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Monitor treats to be less than 10% of daily calories ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 5, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Regular vet checks to establish ideal weight targets and catch weight gain early", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}], "listType": "number", "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null, "textFormat": 1}}, "heading": "Weight Management", "subheading": "Maintaining ideal weight is the #1 factor"}, {"id": "68f186f42b163d67b2257760", "icon": "docs", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Why It Matters", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": ": ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "Maintaining an ideal body weight throughout your dog's entire life is one of the most critical factors in joint health prevention. Excess weight puts additional mechanical stress on joints, increases inflammation throughout the body, acce