e"}]}]}], "maxWidth": "872px", "blockName": "", "blockType": "tabbedTable", "textColor": "#FFFFFF", "borderColor": "#000000", "inactiveTextColor": "#000000", "cellBackgroundColor": "#FCB5A4", "headerBackgroundColor": "#EE6C4D"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "PREVENTION & EARLY DETECTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Joint health problems often develop silently long before dogs show obvious signs of discomfort, making early prevention crucial for maintaining your dog's mobility throughout their life. Prevention of aging starts early in your dog’s life. Proactive care during puppyhood and young adulthood can prevent or significantly delay the onset of joint problems later in life. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is a fundamental shift in veterinary medicine to move from reactive treatment to proactive prevention, especially during a puppy’s critical developmental window. Research from UC Davis tracking over 35,000 dogs across multiple breeds demonstrates that environmental factors during the first 18 months can influence joint health outcomes for a dog's entire lifetime. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "While we cannot prevent all joint problems due to genetic factors, we can significantly influence their severity and timing through proactive care. The goal is to maximize both the quantity and quality of your dog's active years. The most effective joint health prevention plan combines multiple strategies:", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f186cf577f756260829d51", "items": [{"id": "68f186d12b163d67b225775e", "icon": "balance", "content": {"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Why It Matters", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": ": ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "Maintaining an ideal body weight throughout your dog's entire life is one of the most critical factors in joint health prevention. Excess weight puts additional mechanical stress on joints, increases inflammation throughout the body, accelerates cartilage breakdown, and significantly worsens arthritis progression.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"type": "linebreak", "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": "What You Can Do", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 1, "version": 1}, {"mode": "normal", "text": ": ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0