95"}, {"id": "69027194b2441c47b2e648d5", "value": "2605"}]}], "columns": [{"id": "6901100a427e8663653e2c1d", "type": "text", "heading": "Dog weight (lbs)"}, {"id": "69011031427e8663653e2c1f", "type": "text", "heading": "Calories per day for less active (K=80)"}, {"id": "69011037427e8663653e2c21", "type": "text", "heading": "Calories per day for active (K=110)"}], "blockName": "", "blockType": "table", "tableColor": "rgba(255, 161, 47, 0.7)", "tableTitle": "", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "columnHeadingColor": "#FFA12F"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "690271a580904634a4c8b578", "items": [], "heading": "RESOURCES", "blockName": "", "blockType": "collectionItemSlider", "usePlaceholders": true, "widthConstraint": false, "placeholderCount": 5, "placeholderImage": 2, "placeholderTitle": "Placeholder element"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "690271c780904634a4c8b579", "heading": "DID YOU MAKE THIS RECIPE?", "showIcon": true, "blockName": "", "blockType": "instagram", "paragraph": "Share a pic and tag @thedoggydish on Instagram", "textColor": "#FFFFFF", "backgroundColor": "#F6A944"}, "format": "", "version": 2}], "direction": null}}	f
1	604	3313	Description	68f6a8d726db544f3b5707c2	{"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "DESCRIPTION", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "From the athletic agility dog to the couch potato, all dogs will face some degree of joint health challenges. Joints are what connects two or more bones together, and they exist all over the body including the hips, elbows, spine, and jaw. Much like humans, the cartilage can break down with age and injury leading to inflammation and bony changes in and surrounding the joint. The muscles, tendon, and ligaments supporting that joint can also face age and injury-related disease. As a dog parent, this can manifest as a variety of clinical signs both obvious and not. Obvious signs may include limping, slowing down, and stiffness to rise, while less obvious changes may include hesitancy to use stairs, behavior changes such as aggression, altered posturing for urinating and defecating, or a decreased appetite. All of these signs exemplify the importance of joint health in your dog’s life. ", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "While joint diseases such as arthritis are extremely common, there are many, multimodal ways of proactively improving joint health and supporting disease. This includes but is not limited to environmental and lifestyle modifications, physical therapy and rehabilitation, joint-supportive diet and supplements, appropriate exercise, integrative therapies and modalities, platelet-rich plasma and stem cell therapy injections, pharmaceuticals and analgesics, bracing, and surgery. These therapies work synergistically - meaning oftentimes their use together provides stronger benefits than any therapy alone.", "type": "text", "style": "", "detail": 0, "format": 0, "version": 1}], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f94a60a02d68ff6ad8982f", "items": [], "heading": "Resources", "blockName": "", "blockType": "collectionItemSlider", "usePlaceholders": true, "widthConstraint": false, "placeholderCount": 5, "placeholderImage": 2, "placeholderTitle": "Placeholder Element"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}, {"type": "block", "fields": {"id": "68f811d9d470650a3cc9b0c6", "heading": "DID YOU MAKE THIS RECIPE?", "showIcon": true, "blockName": "", "blockType": "instagram", "paragraph": "Share a pic and tag @thedoggydish on Instagram", "textColor": "#FFFFFF", "backgroundColor": "#FFA12F"}, "format": "", "version": 2}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [], "direction": null, "textStyle": "", "textFormat": 0}], "direction": null}}	f
